{
  "version": 1,
  "claim": "In the simulator, torque-mode force realisation error is purely motor cogging (0.333 N sin(50 theta)); a joint offline fit of per-motor force ripple (+ direction offset) with anchors and line stiffness reaches 0.16 +- 0.06 mm on the HP3 ellipsoid (11 runs) and 0.74 +- 0.21 mm on HP5r (6 runs) without configured stiffness or the probe, robust to 2-4x larger ripple; constant per-motor force offset/scale is unobservable from sweep data and shifts top z 3-13 mm.",
  "scope": "Simulation only; offline refit wrapper, not production code; HP3 ellipsoid and HP5r. One HP5r seed unscored.",
  "limitations": [
    "The cogging model is sim-specific; unknown three-harmonic pattern gives 0.66 mm",
    "HP5r keeps +0.4-0.9 mm top-z bias",
    "Fit CPU 25-120 min for HP5r",
    "HP5r collection fails at 2x cogging",
    "Constant offset/scale needs external calibration on hardware"
  ],
